    <h1 class="item-text" >News</h1>
</div>
<div id="panel-1" class="tabs-panel clearfix tab-type-homepage-news-listing without-images " >
    
    <div class="profile-listing-container  profile-news-listing-container profile-news-listing-option-2  profile-news-listing-option-2 clearfix"><div class="profile-tabbed-listing profile-news-listing  without-images clearfix" data-total-results="9">
<div class="grid">
        <div class="col-xs-12 col-m-6 col-lg-4">
	<a href="https://www.denvergov.org/Government/Agencies-Departments-Offices/Agencies-Departments-Offices-Directory/Mayors-Office/News/2026/Mayor-Mike-Johnston-Announces-DOTI-Leadership-Transition" class="profile-list item-0 homepage-show" >		
		<h2>Mayor Mike Johnston Announces DOTI Leadership Transition</h2>
		<p class="published-on small-text">Published on November 02, 2026</p>
		<p>Mayor Mike Johnston today announced that Amy Ford will depart the role of Executive Director of the Department of Transportation & Infrastructure (DOTI), following three years of service to the city. DOTI Chief Operating Officer Cindy Patton will serve as Interim Executive Director.</p>
	</a>
</div><div class="col-xs-12 col-m-6 col-lg-4">
	<a href="https://www.denvergov.org/Government/Agencies-Departments-Offices/Agencies-Departments-Offices-Directory/Department-of-Transportation-and-Infrastructure/News-Outreach/2026-News/DOTI-Travel-Advisory-Oct-30" class="profile-list item-1 homepage-show" >		
		<h2>DOTI Travel Advisory</h2>
		<p class="published-on small-text">Published on October 30, 2026</p>
		<p>Denver’s Department of Transportation and Infrastructure (DOTI) would like the public to be aware of upcoming infrastructure improvements that could temporarily impact travel.</p>
	</a>
</div><div class="col-xs-12 col-m-6 col-lg-4">
	<a href="https://www.denvergov.org/Government/Agencies-Departments-Offices/Agencies-Departments-Offices-Directory/Denver-City-Council/News/ccshcedule11022026" class="profile-list item-2 homepage-show" >		
		<h2>Denver City Council Schedule & Hearings — Week of November 2, 2026</h2>
		<p class="published-on small-text">Published on October 29, 2026</p>
		<p>Denver City Council Schedule & Hearings — Week of November 2, 2026</p>
	</a>
</div><div class="col-xs-12 col-m-6 col-lg-4">
	<a href="https://www.denvergov.org/News-articles/2026/DDDA-Approves-Funds-City-to-Launch-Process-to-Select-Operator-for-Mile-High-Innovation-Program-at-Independence-Plaza" class="profile-list item-3 homepage-show" >		
		<h2>City to Select Operator for Mile High Innovation Program</h2>
		<p class="published-on small-text">Published on October 28, 2026</p>
		<p>The Denver Downtown Development Authority (DDDA or DDA) today announced that it has unanimously approved up to $3.5 million through the DDDA’s $40M Open Denver fund for the city to engage an operator to manage the new Mile High Innovation Program at Independence Plaza. The operator will be selected through the city’s competitive procurement process, led by DEDO.</p>
	</a>
</div><div class="col-xs-12 col-m-6 col-lg-4">
	<a href="https://www.denvergov.org/Government/Agencies-Departments-Offices/Agencies-Departments-Offices-Directory/Community-Planning-and-Development/CPD-News-and-Events/CPD-News/2026/CPD-Blog-Sound-the-Alarm-for-Denver’s-Historic-Firehouses" class="profile-list item-4 homepage-show" >		
		<h2>CPD Blog: Sound the Alarm for Denver’s Historic Firehouses</h2>
		<p class="published-on small-text">Published on October 27, 2026</p>
		<p>Firehouses built across Denver represent unique styles of architecture, chart the progress of the city’s firefighting equipment, and commemorate milestones in civil rights and our community history. Of the 39 firehouses across Denver, eight are designated as historic landmarks.</p>
	</a>
</div><div class="col-xs-12 col-m-6 col-lg-4">
	<a href="https://www.denvergov.org/Government/Agencies-Departments-Offices/Agencies-Departments-Offices-Directory/Public-Health-Environment/DDPHE-Healthy-Insights/Blogs/Proposed-Census-Changes" class="profile-list item-5 homepage-show" >		
		<h2>DDPHE Blog: Make Your Voice Heard on Proposed Census Changes</h2>
		<p class="published-on small-text">Published on October 27, 2026</p>
		<p>The census and American Community Survey provide essential data that guide funding and policy decisions in Denver for an entire decade. Proposed federal changes would exclude many noncitizens from the count and limit key demographic questions, breaking long-standing constitutional precedent and risking significant underrepresentation of Denver’s communities.</p>
	</a>
</div><div class="col-xs-12 col-m-6 col-lg-4">
	<a href="https://www.denvergov.org/Government/Agencies-Departments-Offices/Agencies-Departments-Offices-Directory/Department-of-Transportation-and-Infrastructure/News-Outreach/2026-News/Completion-of-High-Line-Canal-Underpass-at-Yale-Avenue" class="profile-list item-6 homepage-show" >		
		<h2>Completion of High Line Canal Underpass at Yale Avenue</h2>
		<p class="published-on small-text">Published on October 27, 2026</p>
		<p>Representatives from Denver, Arapahoe County and community partners celebrated the completion of the High Line Canal Trail underpass at East Yale Avenue and Holly Street. The new underpass allows people walking and biking along the trail to travel beneath Yale Avenue without crossing vehicle traffic at street level.</p>
	</a>
</div><div class="col-xs-12 col-m-6 col-lg-4">
	<a href="https://www.denvergov.org/Government/Agencies-Departments-Offices/Agencies-Departments-Offices-Directory/Public-Health-Environment/DDPHE-Healthy-Insights/Blogs/DDPHE-Blog-Stay-Ahead-of-Rodents-this-Winter" class="profile-list item-7 homepage-show" >		
		<h2>DDPHE Blog: Stay Ahead of Rodents this Winter</h2>
		<p class="published-on small-text">Published on October 26, 2026</p>
		<p>s temperatures drop, rodents look for warm places to live. Homes, garages, sheds and businesses can become inviting places for mice and rats to settle in for the colder months.</p>
	</a>
</div><div class="col-xs-12 col-m-6 col-lg-4">
